{
  "format": "zapterm-command-lists",
  "version": 1,
  "platform": "fortigate",
  "notes": "FortiGate (FortiOS 7.6) command lists. Every command below was checked against Fortinet's FortiOS 7.6 documentation — nothing was added from memory: • CLI troubleshooting cheat sheet (7.6.0) docs.fortinet.com/document/fortigate/7.6.0/cli-troubleshooting-cheat-sheet/420966 • Administration guide 7.6.6: \"Debugging the packet flow\" (54688), \"IPsec related diagnose commands\" (44240), \"Performing a sniffer trace or packet capture\" (680228: \"To stop the sniffer, type CTRL+C\"), \"Routing concepts\" (139692), \"Using a session table\" (562859), \"How the FortiGate firmware license works\" (7.6.4, 299518) • CLI reference 7.6.6: diagnose vpn ike (309172113), diagnose sys (235530229), diagnose ip router bgp (869760727) / ospf (929006518) Left out on purpose: commands that reset, format or reboot the device (factoryreset, formatlogdisk, execute reboot…), ones the docs warn can cause an outage (execute fsso refresh, diagnose sys ha reset-uptime), ones that put a password on the command line (diagnose test authserver), and ones whose 7.6 argument syntax the docs don't spell out.",
  "label": "FortiGate · FortiOS 7.6",
  "stopDebug": ["diagnose debug disable", "diagnose debug reset"],
  "stopKeys": "\u0003",
